ich is in Phase 2a clinical trials for the treatment of prostate cancer; and Phase 2a clinical trials for the treatment of non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). The company is also developing CAN-3110, which is in Phase Ib clinical trials for the treatment of recurrent high-grade glioma. In addition, it develops the enLIGHTEN Discovery Platform, a systematic, iterative herpes simplex virus based discovery platform leveraging human biology and advanced analytics to create new viral immunotherapy candidates for solid tumors. The company was formerly known as Advantagene, Inc. and changed its name to Candel Therapeutics, Inc. in November 2020. Candel Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2003 and is headquartered in Needham, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Paul-Peter  Tak FOCIS, M.D., Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 55 people. Stock-based compensation of $69K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Candel Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $670M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","The company is burning through $39M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -22.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev"